{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maximumClique","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximumclique()"]}],"metadata":{"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","title":"maximumClique()","symbolKind":"method","roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maximumClique"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"MaximumClique.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Cliques\/MaximumClique.swift#L87"},"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P7CliquesE13maximumCliqueSay6VertexQzGyF","modules":[{"name":"Cliques","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"role":"symbol"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically least largest clique by vertex index, in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order; [] for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"empty graph. Self-loops and parallel edges are ignored. Each largest clique is searched for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from its first vertex v in degeneracy order, among v’s later neighbors, so memory stays O(n +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"m + degeneracy²) however large a hub’s degree; of two cliques of one size, the lesser is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one holding the least vertex of their symmetric difference. For each v, a witness clique W"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(any one of the right size) guides a pass over the candidates in ascending number: a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"candidate in W is taken, any other is taken exactly when a search finds the rest of a clique"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"among the common neighbors left (which then becomes W). A v whose candidates all exceed the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"least vertex of the best clique so far is skipped. Exponential in the worst case."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximumClique()"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximumClique()":{"title":"maximumClique()","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximumclique()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maximumClique"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically least largest clique by vertex index, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order; [] for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"empty graph. Self-loops and parallel edges are ignored. Each largest clique is searched for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from its first vertex v in degeneracy order, among v’s later neighbors, so memory stays O(n +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"m + degeneracy²) however large a hub’s degree; of two cliques of one size, the lesser is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one holding the least vertex of their symmetric difference. For each v, a witness clique W"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(any one of the right size) guides a pass over the candidates in ascending number: a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"candidate in W is taken, any other is taken exactly when a search finds the rest of a clique"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"among the common neighbors left (which then becomes W). A v whose candidates all exceed the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"least vertex of the best clique so far is skipped. Exponential in the worst case."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximumClique()","role":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols":{"abstract":[],"title":"GraphProtocols","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Vertex":{"abstract":[],"title":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph\/vertex","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable"}]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/Graph